{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdyCiB4JbVPppccEVihqA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Audit Conclusion: T6S2 Payroll Engine Golden-Snapshot Gate\n\n## Assessment\n\n**1. Gate design is acceptable as-is; no changes required; second-major proof is NOT required.**\n\n**Rationale:**\n\n- **Documented decision predates the concern.** ADR 007 (2026-03-02) explicitly pins the runtime to Node 20.x and declares the numeric contract: *bitwise reproducibility under a single runtime*. This decision was recorded long before any gate incident and reflects operational intent, not post-hoc silence.\n\n- **The claim is environment-specific, not portable.** The ADR does not claim portability across Node majors. It claims *reproducibility within Node 20*. The baseline frozen under Node 20 correctly inherits Node 20's FP behavior; a pass under Node 20 proves the snapshot matches itself under its declared environment.\n\n- **Teammate's demand misapplies the portability rule.** Per the governing doctrine: \"A baseline claimed portable across supported environments proves that claim on a second, relevantly different one.\" This baseline makes no such claim. Proving it on Node 21+ would test a promise that was never made and would be a misuse of the gate as a de facto portability proof.\n\n- **Full-precision serialization is consistent with the contract.** The `npv` field at full float precision is appropriate *given* the documented pin. If the product moves to multi-runtime support, the numeric contract changes: at that point, a tolerance or canonicalization rule must be added to the comparator (not the production code), and the baseline must be re-proved on the second environment.\n\n- **Current green status is valid.** The gate has been green all year under the declared environment (Node 20, CI + production aligned). No incident has occurred.\n\n**Conclusion:** Close the flag. Document (if not already explicit) that gate portability is out-of-scope until the runtime pin changes. If Node 20 EOL approaches and multi-runtime support becomes necessary, the ADR review and numeric contract adjustment are the remediation path—not retroactive proof on a second major."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":738,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":478,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
